      "semantics": [
        "Applies GroupNorm: for each batch sample and group, compute mean and variance over spatial dimensions, normalize, then apply affine transform with per-channel weight and bias.",
        "Groups are contiguous chunks of channels: group i covers channels [i*C/G, (i+1)*C/G).",
        "Mean and variance are computed over all elements in the group (including spatial dimensions).",
        "Normalization: (x - mean) / sqrt(var + eps).",
        "Affine: y = normalized * weight[channel] + bias[channel].",
        "Input may be non-contiguous; implement using strides or explicit contiguous materialization.",
        "Output tensor has same shape and dtype as input, allocated on CUDA."
      ]
